A keymap change reported as a keyboard layout change (Task 29 of docs/plans/20261023-upstream-sync-v0.38.1.md).
GPUI calls `on_keyboard_layout_change` on Linux only when the effective layout's name differs from the one it noted,
so a new keymap that only adds or drops layouts (`setxkbmap -layout us,ru` on X11; on Wayland a compositor's new
`wl_keyboard.keymap` after its layout list changed, the first layout still selected) reaches no observer. The
keyboard-layout lock re-reads the enabled layouts on that callback, as upstream observes macOS's enabled input
sources. The X11 client's new-keymap events (`XkbNewKeyboardNotify`, `XkbMapNotify`) and the Wayland keyboard's
`Keymap` event now report the change whatever the effective layout's name; a group change still reports only a new
name. GPUI's own observer re-reads the layout and the keyboard mapper on it, which a new keymap changes too. The other
platforms are unchanged. scripts/vendor-gpui.sh applies this to the verified crates.io archive.

